module bindings.rust.zip_member_write_without_containment;

// The zip crate hands the extracting code whatever the archive declares:
// by_index and by_name are the documented member reads that yield each
// ZipFile in turn, and name/name_raw read back the member path the
// archive's own bytes chose -- attacker-controlled text that the crate's
// own documentation warns against using for extraction. std's join keeps
// every parent-directory component such a value carries -- an absolute
// name replaces the base outright, a `..` component walks the join out of
// the directory -- so a manual extraction loop that joins the member name
// onto a destination directory and creates a file or directory there lets
// the archive decide where the bytes land, with the extracting process's
// privileges (CWE-22). The convenience API is the other discipline:
// ZipArchive::extract sanitizes member names itself, and a loop over it
// never reads a member name at all.
//
// The loop is recognised by its documented parts together: a member read
// (by_index/by_name), the member name (name/name_raw), the destination
// join, and a by-name write -- a file or directory create, a copy into a
// created file, or an OpenOptions builder chain. A member read alone is a
// read-only walk (listing an archive's contents, hashing members), and a
// join plus write alone is any file-writing code, from cache builders to
// download savers -- the archive read is what makes it an extraction loop.
//
// The neutralising forms are the crate's own safe-name accessors and
// std's containment vocabulary: enclosed_name is the documented
// safe-to-use form (it rejects absolute paths and `..` escapes outright),
// sanitized_name and mangled_name rewrite the path ignoring components
// with special meaning, and starts_with/strip_prefix against the base, a
// components() walk, canonicalize, or an is_absolute test are std's
// containment routes. Any of these in the function means the member name
// was reduced or checked before use, which is what the review flag asks
// about.
//
// The member reads and the name accessors are matched exactly, not by
// substring: by_name as a substring also reads a store's find_by_name
// lookup (measured -- a fixture-writing test carrying such a lookup was
// the one off-tree hit the substring form produced). The exact form does
// not reach the crate's later *_decrypt member reads, stated rather than
// silently widened.
//
// Residual, stated rather than hidden: the containment test is by call
// name, so a hand-rolled dot-segment rejection over the name's bytes is
// invisible and the flag stands -- the reduction has to go through a
// named API to be seen, and a guard spelled inside an assert!-style
// macro wrapper contributes no call token (measured -- a starts_with
// containment inside assert! did not neutralise), so the containment has
// to sit on a plain statement to be seen. The member read and the join
// are co-located in one function but their arguments are not unified, so
// a function that reads members for one purpose while writing a locally
// built path can still match -- the archive read plus the join plus the
// write is the evidence the flag carries. And a loop split across a
// reader function and a writer function reports nothing here, the
// standard delegation limit.
binding zipMemberWriteWithoutContainment {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "rust" and node.context.call in ["by_index", "by_name"] and node.context.call in ["name", "name_raw"] and node.context.call == "join" and containsAny(node.context.callPath, ["File.create", "create_dir_all", "fs.create_dir", "fs.write", "fs.copy", "fs.rename", "fs.hard_link", "fs.symlink", "write.open", "append.open", "create.open", "truncate.open"]) and not containsAny(node.context.call, ["enclosed_name", "mangled_name", "starts_with", "strip_prefix", "components", "canonicalize", "is_absolute", "sanitize"]) and not containsAny(node.context.callPath, ["ParentDir", "CurDir"]) and not (node.token contains "\"..\"") and not (node.token contains "\".\"")
  emit issue code.ManualZipEntryFileWrite at node
}
